      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village was originally founded as Main Creek before being renamed Conrath.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conrath%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Conrath brothers started a logging and sawmill operation here in 1904 when the area was known as Main Creek Siding.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://ruskcounty.org/?SEC=D2EEB27E-3CA0-422B-BA6D-1AD52BD6E986&DE=2C529EAE-5462-4A30-BAC5-EED8E3DCFCE4"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Historic buildings nominated for the National Register of Historic Places in Conrath include the Spooner House and the Holy Trinity Catholic Church.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
